# SwiftFormat (https://github.com/nicklockwood/SwiftFormat). `make format` rewrites, `make lint`
# only checks. The options mirror the style the code already has.
# The app builds with Xcode 16 (Swift 6.0) and later (README), in the Swift 5 language mode
# (SWIFT_VERSION = 5.0): no rewrite may need a newer compiler.
--swift-version 6.0
--language-mode 5
# BRIQKit/Sources/BRIQKit/Auto-Generated is written by briq-utils: a reformat would be undone by its
# next run.
--exclude BRIQ.xcodeproj,build,**/.build,BRIQKit/Sources/BRIQKit/Auto-Generated

--indent 4
# The code does not indent inside `#if` blocks.
--ifdef no-indent
--max-width 120
# Trailing commas in multi-line collection literals only, as SwiftLint's trailing_comma checks;
# not in argument and parameter lists.
--trailing-commas collections-only
--semicolons never
--ranges no-space
# Digits grouped from five on (`10_000`), so that years stay `1984`.
--decimal-grouping 3,5
--import-grouping testable-bottom
--strip-unused-args closure-only
--wrap-arguments preserve
--wrap-parameters preserve
--wrap-collections preserve
--extension-acl on-extension
# The code writes `case .success(let count)`.
--pattern-let inline
--enable isEmpty
# The code keeps short bodies on one line (`guard x else { return }`) and writes `try` next to the
# call it belongs to. Test functions keep their camelCase names: from Swift 6.2 on,
# swiftTestingTestCaseNames turns them into raw identifiers
# (`` `reports progress once for A single batch` ``).
--disable wrapIfStatementBodies,wrapIfExpressionBodies,wrapLoopBodies,wrapFunctionBodies,wrapPropertyBodies,hoistTry,swiftTestingTestCaseNames
